sentences.l:
“Father Zeus, and you other blessed gods who are forever,
let no longer any ready-minded, gentle and kind sceptre-holding king be,
nor knowing in his mind what is fitting,
but let him always be harsh, and do reckless things;

but he lies on the island, suffering harsh pains,
in the halls of the nymph Calypso, who by constraint
holds him;

he sped then over the wave, like a gull, a bird,
which, along the dread gulfs of the unharvested salt-sea,
hunting fish, wets its close-packed wings in the brine;

A great fire on the hearth was burning, and far off a fragrance,
of easily-split cedar and of citron-wood, throughout the island was wafting,
as they burned;
